{"seconds": 54.3, "exit": 0, "final": "After fxe6, we have Nf7+ and the position is still good for us. The main line with Ke8 is cleanest.\n\n---\n\n**Best move:** Ne6+\n\n**Main line:** Ne6+ Ke8, Nxg7+ Qxg7, Rxd5\n\n**Motif:** fork (the knight on e6 checks the king and attacks the loose knight d5, and after Nxg7+ we win material)\n\n**Coaching note:**\nBlack's queen on f6 and loose knight on d5 created a fatal weakness. Ne6+ forks the king and seals Black's fate: after the forced Ke8, Nxg7+ wins the g7 pawn with check, Black's best try is Qxg7, but then Rxd5 captures the loose knight, leaving White up significant material. **Lesson:** Watch for forcing checks that attack loose pieces\u2014they often lead to immediate tactical wins.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Ne6+\", \"line\": [\"Ne6+\", \"Ke8\", \"Nxg7+\", \"Qxg7\", \"Rxd5\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r2k3r/pppb1ppp/5q2/n2nN3/3N1B2/8/PPP1BPPP/3R1RK1 w - - 4 16"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r2k3r/pppb1ppp/5q2/n2nN3/3N1B2/8/PPP1BPPP/3R1RK1 w - - 4 16"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "r2k3r/pppb1ppp/5q2/n2nN3/3N1B2/8/PPP1BPPP/3R1RK1 w - - 4 16"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2k3r/pppb1ppp/5q2/n2nN3/3N1B2/8/PPP1BPPP/3R1RK1 w - - 4 16", "move": "Nxf7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2k3r/pppb1ppp/5q2/n2nN3/3N1B2/8/PPP1BPPP/3R1RK1 w - - 4 16", "move": "Nec6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2k3r/pppb1ppp/5q2/n2nN3/3N1B2/8/PPP1BPPP/3R1RK1 w - - 4 16", "move": "Ne6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2k3r/pppb1Npp/5q2/n2n4/3N1B2/8/PPP1BPPP/3R1RK1 b - - 0 16", "move": "Qxf7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2k3r/pppb1ppp/4Nq2/n2nN3/5B2/8/PPP1BPPP/3R1RK1 b - - 5 16", "move": "Bxe6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2k3r/ppp2